# OksaSDR tour, "On the air": 80 m SSB in the evening, LSB with the 2.9 kHz receive filter
# (the user: phone always with 2.9 kHz). The radio recalls each band's last mode, so LSB is
# chosen from the mode list (80 m was left in DIGU). Five active frequencies, 20 s each; the
# video keeps the best (the others !cut in the log). Receive only.
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # On the air
caption Each mode as it sounds on the band right now, live from the radio.
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption SSB on 80 m in the evening: tap the frequency and type it.
caption !mark 240,145
frequency-dialog
wait 1500
keys 3.650
wait 1500
keys <Enter>
wait 1500
span 10
wait 2000
caption Then the mode: LSB, the sideband of the low bands.
taptext DIGU
wait 2000
taptext LSB
wait 2500
caption Phone sounds fuller with the 2.9 kHz receive filter: tap the filter width, then 2.9k.
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 2000
taptext 2.9k
wait 2000
close
wait 1000
caption @ssb 3.650
caption 80 m SSB at 3.650 MHz, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
wait 20000
caption @ssb 3.641
caption 80 m SSB at 3.641 MHz, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
freq 3.641
span 10
wait 20000
caption @ssb 3.695
caption 80 m SSB at 3.695 MHz, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
freq 3.695
span 10
wait 20000
caption @ssb 3.743
caption 80 m SSB at 3.743 MHz, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
freq 3.743
span 10
wait 20000
caption @ssb 3.750
caption 80 m SSB at 3.750 MHz, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
freq 3.750
span 10
wait 20000
caption @ssb end
caption -
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
slices
